  {
    "id" : "flowtype_array-style-complex-type",
    "level" : "Info",
    "category" : "CodeStyle",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Enforce Flowtype Array Style for Complex Types",
    "description" : "Enforces consistent annotation style for complex array types in Flowtype, either using 'Array<Type>' or 'Type[]'.",
    "explanation" : "### `array-style-complex-type`\n\n_The `--fix` option on the command line automatically fixes problems reported by this rule._\n\nEnforces a particular annotation style of complex types.\n\nType is considered complex in these cases:\n\n* [Maybe type](https://flow.org/en/docs/types/maybe/)\n* [Function type](https://flow.org/en/docs/types/functions/)\n* [Object type](https://flow.org/en/docs/types/objects/)\n* [Tuple type](https://flow.org/en/docs/types/tuples/)\n* [Union type](https://flow.org/en/docs/types/unions/)\n* [Intersection type](https://flow.org/en/docs/types/intersections/)\n\nThis rule takes one argument.\n\nIf it is `'verbose'` then a problem is raised when using `Type[]` instead of `Array<Type>`.\n\nIf it is `'shorthand'` then a problem is raised when using `Array<Type>` instead of `Type[]`.\n\nThe default value is `'verbose'`.\n\n<!-- assertions arrayStyleComplexType -->",
    "enabled" : false,
    "timeToFix" : 3,
    "parameters" : [
    ],
    "languages" : [
    ]
  },
  {
    "id" : "flowtype_array-style-simple-type",
    "level" : "Info",
    "category" : "CodeStyle",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Enforce Flowtype Array Style for Simple Types",
    "description" : "Enforces a consistent array type annotation style for simple types in Flowtype, either using shorthand (Type[]) or verbose (Array<Type>) notation.",
    "explanation" : "### `array-style-simple-type`\n\n_The `--fix` option on the command line automatically fixes problems reported by this rule._\n\nEnforces a particular array type annotation style of simple types.\n\nType is considered simple in these cases:\n\n* [Primitive types](https://flow.org/en/docs/types/primitives/)\n* [Literal types](https://flow.org/en/docs/types/literals/)\n* [Mixed type](https://flow.org/en/docs/types/mixed/)\n* [Any type](https://flow.org/en/docs/types/any/)\n* [Class type](https://flow.org/en/docs/types/classes/)\n* [Generic type](https://flow.org/en/docs/types/generics/)\n* Array type [shorthand notation](https://flow.org/en/docs/types/arrays/#toc-array-type-shorthand-syntax)\n\nThis rule takes one argument.\n\nIf it is `'verbose'` then a problem is raised when using `Type[]` instead of `Array<Type>`.\n\nIf it is `'shorthand'` then a problem is raised when using `Array<Type>` instead of `Type[]`.\n\nThe default value is `'verbose'`.\n\n<!-- assertions arrayStyleSimpleType -->",
    "enabled" : false,
    "timeToFix" : 5,
    "parameters" : [
    ],
    "languages" : [
    ]
  },
  {
    "id" : "flowtype_arrow-parens",
    "level" : "Info",
    "category" : "CodeStyle",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Enforce Parentheses Around Arrow Function Arguments",
    "description" : "This rule enforces consistent use of parentheses around arguments in arrow functions in JavaScript/Flowtype code.",
    "explanation" : "### `arrow-parens`\n\n_The `--fix` option on the command line automatically fixes problems reported by this rule._\n\nEnforces the consistent use of parentheses in arrow functions.\n\nThis rule has a string option and an object one.\n\nString options are:\n\n- `\"always\"` (default) requires parens around arguments in all cases.\n- `\"as-needed\"` enforces no braces where they can be omitted.\n\nObject properties for variants of the `\"as-needed\"` option:\n\n- `\"requireForBlockBody\": true` modifies the as-needed rule in order to require parens if the function body is in an instructions block (surrounded by braces).\n\n<!-- assertions arrowParens -->",
    "enabled" : false,
    "timeToFix" : 3,
    "parameters" : [
      {
        "name" : "unnamedParam",
        "default" : "always",
        "description" : "unnamedParam"
      }
    ],
    "languages" : [
    ]
  },
  {
    "id" : "flowtype_boolean-style",
    "level" : "Info",
    "category" : "CodeStyle",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Enforce Flowtype Boolean Style",
    "description" : "Enforces consistent style for boolean type annotations in Flowtype, requiring either 'boolean' or 'bool' consistently.",
    "explanation" : "### `boolean-style`\n\n_The `--fix` option on the command line automatically fixes problems reported by this rule._\n\nEnforces a particular style for boolean type annotations. This rule takes one argument.\n\nIf it is `'boolean'` then a problem is raised when using `bool` instead of `boolean`.\n\nIf it is `'bool'` then a problem is raised when using `boolean` instead of `bool`.\n\nThe default value is `'boolean'`.\n\n<!-- assertions booleanStyle -->",
    "enabled" : false,
    "timeToFix" : 5,
    "parameters" : [
    ],
    "languages" : [
    ]
  },
  {
    "id" : "flowtype_define-flow-type",
    "level" : "Info",
    "category" : "BestPractice",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Mark Flow Type Identifiers as Defined",
    "description" : "Marks Flow type identifiers as defined to prevent ESLint's no-undef rule from reporting them as undefined.",
    "explanation" : "### `define-flow-type`\n\nMarks Flow type identifiers as defined.\n\nUsed to suppress [`no-undef`](http://eslint.org/docs/rules/no-undef) reporting of type identifiers.\n\n<!-- assertions defineFlowType -->",
    "enabled" : false,
    "timeToFix" : 5,
    "parameters" : [
    ],
    "languages" : [
    ]
  },
  {
    "id" : "flowtype_delimiter-dangle",
    "level" : "Info",
    "category" : "CodeStyle",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Enforce Consistent Trailing Commas in Flowtype Annotations",
    "description" : "This rule enforces consistent use of trailing commas in Flowtype Object, Tuple, Interface, and inexact object annotations.",
    "explanation" : "### `delimiter-dangle`\n\n_The `--fix` option on the command line automatically fixes problems reported by this rule._\n\nEnforces consistent use of trailing commas in Object and Tuple annotations.\n\nThis rule takes three arguments where the possible values are the same as ESLint's default `comma-dangle` rule:\n\n1. The first argument is for Object and Tuple annotations. The default value is `'never'`.\n2. The second argument is used for Interface annotations. This defaults to the value of the first argument.\n3. The third argument is used for inexact object notation (trailing `...`). The default value is `'never'`.\n\nIf it is `'never'` then a problem is raised when there is a trailing comma.\n\nIf it is `'always'` then a problem is raised when there is no trailing comma.\n\nIf it is `'always-multiline'` then a problem is raised when there is no trailing comma on a multi-line definition, or there _is_ a trailing comma on a single-line definition.\n\nIf it is `'only-multiline'` then a problem is raised when there is a trailing comma on a single-line definition. It allows, but does not enforce, trailing commas on multi-line definitions.\n\n<!-- assertions delimiterDangle -->",
    "enabled" : false,
    "timeToFix" : 3,
    "parameters" : [
    ],
    "languages" : [
    ]
  },
  {
    "id" : "flowtype_enforce-line-break",
    "level" : "Info",
    "category" : "CodeStyle",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Enforce Line Break Between Flowtype Definitions",
    "description" : "This rule enforces line breaks between Flowtype type definitions to improve code readability and maintain consistent formatting.",
    "explanation" : "### `enforce-line-break`\n\nThis rule enforces line breaks between type definitions.\n\n<!-- assertions enforceLineBreak -->",
    "enabled" : false,
    "timeToFix" : 3,
    "parameters" : [
    ],
    "languages" : [
    ]
  },
  {
    "id" : "flowtype_generic-spacing",
    "level" : "Info",
    "category" : "CodeStyle",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Enforce consistent spacing in Flowtype generic parameters",
    "description" : "This rule enforces consistent spacing inside generic type annotation parameters in Flowtype syntax.",
    "explanation" : "### `generic-spacing`\n\n_The `--fix` option on the command line automatically fixes problems reported by this rule._\n\nEnforces consistent spacing within generic type annotation parameters.\n\nThis rule takes one argument. If it is `'never'` then a problem is raised when there is a space surrounding the generic type parameters. If it is `'always'` then a problem is raised when there is no space surrounding the generic type parameters.\n\nThe default value is `'never'`.\n\n<!-- assertions genericSpacing -->",
    "enabled" : false,
    "timeToFix" : 3,
    "parameters" : [
    ],
    "languages" : [
    ]
  },
  {
    "id" : "flowtype_interface-id-match",
    "level" : "Info",
    "category" : "CodeStyle",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Enforce Interface Name Pattern",
    "description" : "Enforces a consistent naming pattern for Flowtype interfaces to ensure interface names match a specified regular expression pattern.",
    "explanation" : "### `interface-id-match`\n\nEnforces a consistent naming pattern for interfaces.\n\n#### Options\n\nThis rule requires a text RegExp:\n\n```js\n{\n    \"rules\": {\n        \"flowtype/interface-id-match\": [\n            2,\n            \"^([A-Z][a-z0-9]*)+Type$\"\n        ]\n    }\n}\n```\n\n`'^([A-Z][a-z0-9]*)+Type$$'` is the default pattern.\n\n<!-- assertions interfaceIdMatch -->",
    "enabled" : false,
    "timeToFix" : 3,
    "parameters" : [
    ],
    "languages" : [
    ]
  },
  {
    "id" : "flowtype_newline-after-flow-annotation",
    "level" : "Info",
    "category" : "CodeStyle",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Enforce Newline After Flow Annotation",
    "description" : "This rule enforces the presence or absence of an empty line immediately after the Flow type annotation comment in JavaScript files.",
    "explanation" : "### `newline-after-flow-annotation`\n\nThis rule requires an empty line after the Flow annotation.\n\n#### Options\n\nThe rule has a string option:\n\n* `\"always\"` (default): Enforces that `@flow` annotations be followed by an empty line, separated by newline (LF)\n* `\"always-windows\"`: Identical to \"always\", but will use a CRLF when autofixing\n* `\"never\"`: Enforces that `@flow` annotations are not followed by empty lines\n\n```js\n{\n  \"rules\": {\n    \"flowtype/newline-after-flow-annotation\": [\n      2,\n      \"always\"\n    ]\n  }\n}\n```\n\n\n<!-- assertions newlineAfterFlowAnnotation -->",
    "enabled" : false,
    "timeToFix" : 2,
    "parameters" : [
    ],
    "languages" : [
    ]
  },
  {
    "id" : "flowtype_no-dupe-keys",
    "level" : "High",
    "category" : "ErrorProne",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Disallow Duplicate Keys in Flowtype Object Annotations",
    "description" : "This rule disallows duplicate property keys in Flowtype object annotations to prevent conflicts and unexpected behavior.",
    "explanation" : "### `no-dupe-keys`\n\nChecks for duplicate properties in Object annotations.\n\nThis rule mirrors ESLint's [no-dupe-keys](http://eslint.org/docs/rules/no-dupe-keys) rule.\n\n```js\n{\n    \"rules\": {\n        \"flowtype/no-dupe-keys\": 2\n    }\n}\n```\n\n<!-- assertions noDupeKeys -->",
    "enabled" : false,
    "timeToFix" : 5,
    "parameters" : [
    ],
    "languages" : [
    ]
  },
  {
    "id" : "flowtype_no-duplicate-type-union-intersection-members",
    "level" : "Warning",
    "category" : "BestPractice",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Disallow Duplicate Members in Flowtype Union and Intersection Types",
    "description" : "This rule checks for and disallows duplicate members within Flowtype union and intersection types to prevent redundancy.",
    "explanation" : "### `no-duplicate-type-union-intersection-members`\n\n_The `--fix` option on the command line automatically fixes problems reported by this rule._\n\nChecks for duplicate members of a type union/intersection.\n\n#### Options\n\nYou can disable checking intersection types using `checkIntersections`.\n\n* `true` (default) - check for duplicate members of intersection members.\n* `false` - do not check for duplicate members of intersection members.\n\n```js\n{\n  \"rules\": {\n    \"flowtype/no-duplicate-type-union-intersection-members\": [\n      2,\n      {\n        \"checkIntersections\": true\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n}\n```\n\nYou can disable checking union types using `checkUnions`.\n\n* `true` (default) - check for duplicate members of union members.\n* `false` - do not check for duplicate members of union members.\n\n```js\n{\n  \"rules\": {\n    \"flowtype/no-duplicate-type-union-intersection-members\": [\n      2,\n      {\n        \"checkUnions\": true\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n}\n```\n\n<!-- assertions noDuplicateTypeUnionIntersectionMembers -->",
    "enabled" : false,
    "timeToFix" : 5,
    "parameters" : [
    ],
    "languages" : [
    ]
