  {
    "id" : "jsx-a11y_click-events-have-key-events",
    "level" : "High",
    "category" : "BestPractice",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Enforce keyboard event handlers with clickable non-interactive elements",
    "description" : "Ensure that clickable non-interactive elements have at least one keyboard event listener to support keyboard accessibility.",
    "explanation" : "# jsx-a11y/click-events-have-key-events\n\n💼 This rule is enabled in the following configs: ☑️ `recommended`, 🔒 `strict`.\n\n<!-- end auto-generated rule header -->\n\nEnforce `onClick` is accompanied by at least one of the following: `onKeyUp`, `onKeyDown`, `onKeyPress`. Coding for the keyboard is important for users with physical disabilities who cannot use a mouse, AT compatibility, and screenreader users. This does not apply for interactive or hidden elements.\n\n## Rule details\n\nThis rule takes no arguments.\n\n### Succeed\n```jsx\n<div onClick={() => {}} onKeyDown={this.handleKeyDown} />\n<div onClick={() => {}} onKeyUp={this.handleKeyUp} />\n<div onClick={() => {}} onKeyPress={this.handleKeyPress} />\n<button onClick={() => {}} />\n<div onClick{() => {}} aria-hidden=\"true\" />\n```\n\n### Fail\n```jsx\n<div onClick={() => {}} />\n```\n\n## Accessibility guidelines\n- [WCAG 2.1.1](https://www.w3.org/WAI/WCAG21/Understanding/keyboard)",
    "enabled" : false,
    "timeToFix" : 5,
    "parameters" : [
    ],
    "languages" : [
    ]
