  {
    "id" : "nuxt_no-env-in-context",
    "level" : "Warning",
    "category" : "BestPractice",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Disallow context.isServer/context.isClient in asyncData/fetch/nuxtServerInit",
    "description" : "This rule disallows the use of context.isServer and context.isClient inside asyncData, fetch, and nuxtServerInit methods in Nuxt.js to prevent misuse of environment detection.",
    "explanation" : "# nuxt/no-env-in-context\n\n> disallow `context.isServer/context.isClient` in `asyncData/fetch/nuxtServerInit`\n\n- :gear: This rule is included in `\"plugin:nuxt/base\"`.\n\n## Rule Details\n\nThis rule is for preventing using `context.isServer/context.isClient` in `asyncData/fetch/nuxtServerInit`\n\nExamples of **incorrect** code for this rule:\n\n```js\n\nexport default {\n  asyncData(context) {\n    if (context.isServer) {\n      const foo = 'bar'\n    }\n  },\n  fetch({ isClient }) {\n    if (isClient) {\n      const foo = 'bar'\n    }\n  }\n}\n\n```\n\nExamples of **correct** code for this rule:\n\n```js\n\nexport default {\n  async asyncData() {\n    if (process.server) {\n      const foo = 'bar'\n    }\n  },\n  fetch() {\n    if (process.client) {\n      const foo = 'bar'\n    }\n  }\n}\n\n```\n\n## :mag: Implementation\n\n- [Rule source](https://github.com/nuxt/eslint-plugin-nuxt/tree/master/lib/rules/no-env-in-context.js)\n- [Test source](https://github.com/nuxt/eslint-plugin-nuxt/tree/master/lib/rules/__tests__/no-env-in-context.test.js)",
    "enabled" : false,
    "timeToFix" : 5,
    "parameters" : [
    ],
    "languages" : [
    ]
  },
  {
    "id" : "nuxt_no-env-in-hooks",
    "level" : "Warning",
    "category" : "BestPractice",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Disallow process.env in client-only Vue lifecycle hooks",
    "description" : "This rule disallows the use of process.server, process.client, and process.browser within specific Vue lifecycle hooks that are only executed on the client side, such as beforeMount, mounted, beforeUpdate, updated, activated, deactivated, beforeDestroy, and destroyed.",
    "explanation" : "# nuxt/no-env-in-hooks\n\n> Disallow `process.server`, `process.client` and `process.browser` in the following lifecycle hooks: `beforeMount`, `mounted`, `beforeUpdate`, `updated`, `activated`, `deactivated`, `beforeDestroy` and `destroyed`.\n\n- :gear: This rule is included in `\"plugin:nuxt/base\"`.\n\n## Rule Details\n\nThis rule is for preventing using `process.server`/`process.client`/`process.browser` in client only Vue lifecycle hooks since they're only executed in client side.\n\nExamples of **incorrect** code for this rule:\n\n```js\n\nexport default {\n  mounted() {\n    if (process.server) {\n      const foo = 'bar'\n    }\n  },\n  beforeMount() {\n    if (process.client) {\n      const foo = 'bar'\n    }\n  },\n  beforeDestroy() {\n    if (process.browser) {\n      const foo = 'bar'\n    }\n  }\n}\n\n```\n\nExamples of **correct** code for this rule:\n\n\n```js\n\nexport default {\n  mounted() {\n    const foo = 'bar'\n  },\n  beforeMount() {\n    const foo = 'bar'\n  },\n  beforeDestroy() {\n    const foo = 'bar'\n  }\n}\n\n```\n\n## :mag: Implementation\n\n- [Rule source](https://github.com/nuxt/eslint-plugin-nuxt/tree/master/lib/rules/no-env-in-hooks.js)\n- [Test source](https://github.com/nuxt/eslint-plugin-nuxt/tree/master/lib/rules/__tests__/no-env-in-hooks.test.js)",
    "enabled" : false,
    "timeToFix" : 5,
    "parameters" : [
    ],
    "languages" : [
    ]
  },
  {
    "id" : "nuxt_no-globals-in-created",
    "level" : "High",
    "category" : "ErrorProne",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Disallow Globals in created/beforeCreate",
    "description" : "This rule disallows the use of global objects like window or document in the created or beforeCreate lifecycle hooks in Nuxt components.",
    "explanation" : "# nuxt/no-globals-in-created\n\n> disallow `window/document` in `created/beforeCreate`\n\n- :gear: This rule is included in `\"plugin:nuxt/base\"`.\n\n## Rule Details\n\nThis rule is for preventing using `window/document` in `created/beforeCreate`, since `created/beforeCreate` may be executed in server side in SSR.\n\nExamples of **incorrect** code for this rule:\n\n```js\n\nexport default {\n  created() {\n    window.foo = 'bar'\n  }\n}\n\n```\n\nExamples of **correct** code for this rule:\n\n```js\n\nexport default {\n  created() {\n    const foo = 'bar'\n  }\n}\n\n```\n\n## :mag: Implementation\n\n- [Rule source](https://github.com/nuxt/eslint-plugin-nuxt/tree/master/lib/rules/no-globals-in-created.js)\n- [Test source](https://github.com/nuxt/eslint-plugin-nuxt/tree/master/lib/rules/__tests__/no-globals-in-created.test.js)",
