    "id" : "regexp_prefer-range",
    "level" : "Info",
    "category" : "CodeStyle",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Enforce Using Character Class Range in Regular Expressions",
    "description" : "This rule enforces the use of character class ranges instead of multiple adjacent characters in regular expressions.",
    "explanation" : "---\npageClass: \"rule-details\"\nsidebarDepth: 0\ntitle: \"regexp/prefer-range\"\ndescription: \"enforce using character class range\"\nsince: \"v0.4.0\"\n---\n# regexp/prefer-range\n\n💼 This rule is enabled in the following configs: 🟢 `flat/recommended`, 🔵 `recommended`.\n\n🔧 This rule is automatically fixable by the [`--fix` CLI option](https://eslint.org/docs/latest/user-guide/command-line-interface#--fix).\n\n<!-- end auto-generated rule header -->\n\n> enforce using character class range\n\n## :book: Rule Details\n\nThis rule is aimed to use ranges instead of multiple adjacent characters in character class.\n\n<eslint-code-block fix>\n\n```js\n/* eslint regexp/prefer-range: \"error\" */\n\n/* ✓ GOOD */\nvar foo = /[0-9]/\nvar foo = /[a-f]/\n\n/* ✗ BAD */\nvar foo = /[123456]/\nvar foo = /[a-cd-f]/\n```\n\n</eslint-code-block>\n\n## :wrench: Options\n\n```json5\n{\n  \"regexp/prefer-range\": [\"error\",\n    {\n      \"target\": \"alphanumeric\" // or \"all\" or [...]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\nThis option can be used to override the [allowedCharacterRanges] setting.\n\nIt allows all values that the [allowedCharacterRanges] setting allows.\n\n[allowedCharacterRanges]: ../settings/index.md#allowedCharacterRanges\n\n### `\"target\": \"alphanumeric\"`\n\n<eslint-code-block fix>\n\n```js\n/* eslint regexp/prefer-range: [\"error\", { \"target\": \"alphanumeric\" }] */\n\n/* ✓ GOOD */\nvar foo = /[0-9]/\nvar foo = /[a-f]/\nvar foo = /[!-$]/\nvar foo = /[!\"#$]/\nvar foo = /[😀-😄]/u\nvar foo = /[😀😁😂😃😄]/u\n\n/* ✗ BAD */\nvar foo = /[123456]/\nvar foo = /[a-cd-f]/\n```\n\n</eslint-code-block>\n\n### `\"target\": \"all\"`\n\n<eslint-code-block fix>\n\n```js\n/* eslint regexp/prefer-range: [\"error\", { \"target\": \"all\" }] */\n\n/* ✓ GOOD */\nvar foo = /[0-9]/\nvar foo = /[a-f]/\nvar foo = /[!-$]/\nvar foo = /[😀-😄]/u\n\n/* ✗ BAD */\nvar foo = /[123456]/\nvar foo = /[a-cd-f]/\nvar foo = /[!\"#$]/\nvar foo = /[😀😁😂😃😄]/u\n```\n\n</eslint-code-block>\n\n### `\"target\": [ \"alphanumeric\", \"😀-😏\" ]`\n\n<eslint-code-block fix>\n\n```js\n/* eslint regexp/prefer-range: [\"error\", { \"target\": [ \"alphanumeric\", \"😀-😏\" ] }] */\n\n/* ✓ GOOD */\nvar foo = /[0-9]/\nvar foo = /[a-f]/\nvar foo = /[!-$]/\nvar foo = /[!\"#$]/\nvar foo = /[😀-😄]/u\n\n/* ✗ BAD */\nvar foo = /[123456]/\nvar foo = /[a-cd-f]/\nvar foo = /[😀😁😂😃😄]/u\n```\n\n</eslint-code-block>\n\n## :rocket: Version\n\nThis rule was introduced in eslint-plugin-regexp v0.4.0\n\n## :mag: Implementation\n\n- [Rule source](https://github.com/ota-meshi/eslint-plugin-regexp/blob/master/lib/rules/prefer-range.ts)\n- [Test source](https://github.com/ota-meshi/eslint-plugin-regexp/blob/master/tests/lib/rules/prefer-range.ts)",
