  {
    "id" : "rxjs_no-subscribe-handlers",
    "level" : "Warning",
    "category" : "BestPractice",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Forbid Passing Handlers to subscribe in RxJS",
    "description" : "This rule forbids passing handler functions or observer objects directly to the RxJS subscribe method.",
    "explanation" : "# Forbid the passing of handlers to `subscribe` (`no-subscribe-handlers`)\n\nThis rule effects failures whenever `subscribe` is called with handlers.\n\n## Rule details\n\nExamples of **incorrect** code for this rule:\n\n```ts\nimport { of } from \"rxjs\";\nimport { tap } from \"rxjs/operators\";\n\nof(42, 54).subscribe((value) => console.log(value));\n```\n\n<!-- prettier-ignore -->\n```ts\nimport { of } from \"rxjs\";\nimport { tap } from \"rxjs/operators\";\n\nof(42, 54).subscribe({\n  next: (value) => console.log(value),\n});\n```\n\nExamples of **correct** code for this rule:\n\n<!-- prettier-ignore -->\n```ts\nimport { of } from \"rxjs\";\n\nof(42, 54)\n  .pipe(tap((value) => console.log(value)))\n  .subscribe();\n```\n\n## Options\n\nThis rule has no options.",
    "enabled" : false,
    "timeToFix" : 5,
    "parameters" : [
    ],
    "languages" : [
    ]
  },
  {
    "id" : "rxjs_no-tap",
    "level" : "Warning",
    "category" : "BestPractice",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Disallow use of RxJS tap operator",
    "description" : "This rule forbids the use of the RxJS `tap` operator in code.",
    "explanation" : "# Avoid `tap` (`no-tap`)\n\nThis rule effects failures if the `tap` operator is used.\n\n## Options\n\nThis rule has no options.",
    "enabled" : false,
