  {
    "id" : "security_detect-no-csrf-before-method-override",
    "level" : "High",
    "category" : "Security",
    "subCategory" : "CSRF",
    "title" : "Detect CSRF Middleware Setup Before Method Override",
    "description" : "Detects if Express 'csrf' middleware is configured before 'method-override' middleware, which can lead to CSRF protection bypass.",
    "explanation" : "# Detects Express \"csrf\" middleware setup before \"method-override\" middleware (`security/detect-no-csrf-before-method-override`)\n\n⚠️ This rule _warns_ in the ✅ `recommended` config.\n\n<!-- end auto-generated rule header -->\n\nThis can allow `GET` requests (which are not checked by `csrf`) to turn into `POST` requests later.\n\nMore information: [Bypass Connect CSRF protection by abusing methodOverride Middleware](https://github.com/eslint-community/eslint-plugin-security/tree/main/docs/bypass-connect-csrf-protection-by-abusing.md)",
