    "title" : "Enforce Vue HTML End Tags",
    "description" : "This rule enforces that HTML elements in Vue templates have proper end tags, disallowing missing end tags where they are required.",
    "explanation" : "---\npageClass: rule-details\nsidebarDepth: 0\ntitle: vue/html-end-tags\ndescription: enforce end tag style\nsince: v3.0.0\n---\n\n# vue/html-end-tags\n\n> enforce end tag style\n\n- :gear: This rule is included in all of `\"plugin:vue/vue3-strongly-recommended\"`, `*.configs[\"flat/strongly-recommended\"]`, `\"plugin:vue/strongly-recommended\"`, `*.configs[\"flat/vue2-strongly-recommended\"]`, `\"plugin:vue/vue3-recommended\"`, `*.configs[\"flat/recommended\"]`, `\"plugin:vue/recommended\"` and `*.configs[\"flat/vue2-recommended\"]`.\n- :wrench: The `--fix` option on the [command line](https://eslint.org/docs/user-guide/command-line-interface#fixing-problems) can automatically fix some of the problems reported by this rule.\n\n## :book: Rule Details\n\nThis rule aims to disallow lacking end tags.\n\n<eslint-code-block fix :rules=\"{'vue/html-end-tags': ['error']}\">\n\n```vue\n<template>\n  <!-- ✓ GOOD -->\n  <div></div>\n  <p></p>\n  <p></p>\n  <input>\n  <br>\n\n  <!-- ✗ BAD -->\n  <div>\n  <p>\n</template>\n```\n\n</eslint-code-block>\n\n## :wrench: Options\n\nNothing.\n\n## :rocket: Version\n\nThis rule was introduced in eslint-plugin-vue v3.0.0\n\n## :mag: Implementation\n\n- [Rule source](https://github.com/vuejs/eslint-plugin-vue/blob/master/lib/rules/html-end-tags.js)\n- [Test source](https://github.com/vuejs/eslint-plugin-vue/blob/master/tests/lib/rules/html-end-tags.js)",
