    "id" : "vue_no-v-html",
    "level" : "High",
    "category" : "Security",
    "subCategory" : "XSS",
    "title" : "Disallow use of v-html directive",
    "description" : "This rule disallows the use of the v-html directive in Vue templates to prevent potential Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) attacks.",
    "explanation" : "---\npageClass: rule-details\nsidebarDepth: 0\ntitle: vue/no-v-html\ndescription: disallow use of v-html to prevent XSS attack\nsince: v4.7.0\n---\n\n# vue/no-v-html\n\n> disallow use of v-html to prevent XSS attack\n\n- :gear: This rule is included in all of `\"plugin:vue/vue3-recommended\"`, `*.configs[\"flat/recommended\"]`, `\"plugin:vue/recommended\"` and `*.configs[\"flat/vue2-recommended\"]`.\n\n## :book: Rule Details\n\nThis rule reports all uses of `v-html` directive in order to reduce the risk of injecting potentially unsafe / unescaped html into the browser leading to Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) attacks.\n\n<eslint-code-block :rules=\"{'vue/no-v-html': ['error']}\">\n\n```vue\n<template>\n  <!-- ✓ GOOD -->\n  <div>{{ someHTML }}</div>\n\n  <!-- ✗ BAD -->\n  <div v-html=\"someHTML\"></div>\n</template>\n```\n\n</eslint-code-block>\n\n## :wrench: Options\n\nNothing.\n\n## :mute: When Not To Use It\n\nIf you are certain the content passed to `v-html` is sanitized HTML you can disable this rule.\n\n## :rocket: Version\n\nThis rule was introduced in eslint-plugin-vue v4.7.0\n\n## :mag: Implementation\n\n- [Rule source](https://github.com/vuejs/eslint-plugin-vue/blob/master/lib/rules/no-v-html.js)\n- [Test source](https://github.com/vuejs/eslint-plugin-vue/blob/master/tests/lib/rules/no-v-html.js)",
    "enabled" : false,
    "timeToFix" : 5,
    "parameters" : [
