    "id" : "vue_valid-attribute-name",
    "level" : "High",
    "category" : "ErrorProne",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Enforce Valid Attribute Names in Vue Templates",
    "description" : "This rule enforces the use of valid HTML attribute names in Vue template elements.",
    "explanation" : "---\npageClass: rule-details\nsidebarDepth: 0\ntitle: vue/valid-attribute-name\ndescription: require valid attribute names\nsince: v9.0.0\n---\n\n# vue/valid-attribute-name\n\n> require valid attribute names\n\n- :gear: This rule is included in all of `\"plugin:vue/vue3-essential\"`, `*.configs[\"flat/essential\"]`, `\"plugin:vue/essential\"`, `*.configs[\"flat/vue2-essential\"]`, `\"plugin:vue/vue3-strongly-recommended\"`, `*.configs[\"flat/strongly-recommended\"]`, `\"plugin:vue/strongly-recommended\"`, `*.configs[\"flat/vue2-strongly-recommended\"]`, `\"plugin:vue/vue3-recommended\"`, `*.configs[\"flat/recommended\"]`, `\"plugin:vue/recommended\"` and `*.configs[\"flat/vue2-recommended\"]`.\n\n## :book: Rule Details\n\nThis rule detects invalid HTML attributes.\n\n<eslint-code-block :rules=\"{'vue/valid-attribute-name': ['error']}\">\n\n```vue\n<template>\n  <!-- ✓ GOOD -->\n  <p foo.bar></p>\n  <p foo-bar></p>\n  <p _foo.bar></p>\n  <p :foo-bar></p>\n\n  <!-- ✗ BAD -->\n  <p 0abc></p>\n  <p -def></p>\n  <p !ghi></p>\n</template>\n```\n\n</eslint-code-block>\n\n## :wrench: Options\n\nNothing.\n\n## :rocket: Version\n\nThis rule was introduced in eslint-plugin-vue v9.0.0\n\n## :mag: Implementation\n\n- [Rule source](https://github.com/vuejs/eslint-plugin-vue/blob/master/lib/rules/valid-attribute-name.js)\n- [Test source](https://github.com/vuejs/eslint-plugin-vue/blob/master/tests/lib/rules/valid-attribute-name.js)",
