  {
    "id" : "vue_valid-model-definition",
    "level" : "High",
    "category" : "ErrorProne",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Enforce valid keys in Vue model option",
    "description" : "This rule enforces that only valid keys are used in the Vue component's model option.",
    "explanation" : "---\npageClass: rule-details\nsidebarDepth: 0\ntitle: vue/valid-model-definition\ndescription: require valid keys in model option\nsince: v9.0.0\n---\n\n# vue/valid-model-definition\n\n> require valid keys in model option\n\n- :gear: This rule is included in all of `\"plugin:vue/essential\"`, `*.configs[\"flat/vue2-essential\"]`, `\"plugin:vue/strongly-recommended\"`, `*.configs[\"flat/vue2-strongly-recommended\"]`, `\"plugin:vue/recommended\"` and `*.configs[\"flat/vue2-recommended\"]`.\n\n## :book: Rule Details\n\nThis rule is aimed at preventing invalid keys in model option.\n\n<eslint-code-block :rules=\"{'vue/valid-model-definition': ['error']}\">\n\n```vue\n<script>\n/* ✓ GOOD */\nexport default {\n  model: {\n    prop: 'list',\n  }\n}\n</script>\n```\n\n</eslint-code-block>\n\n<eslint-code-block :rules=\"{'vue/valid-model-definition': ['error']}\">\n\n```vue\n<script>\n/* ✓ GOOD */\nexport default {\n  model: {\n    event: 'update'\n  }\n}\n</script>\n```\n\n</eslint-code-block>\n\n<eslint-code-block :rules=\"{'vue/valid-model-definition': ['error']}\">\n\n```vue\n<script>\n/* ✓ GOOD */\nexport default {\n  model: {\n    prop: 'list',\n    event: 'update'\n  }\n}\n</script>\n```\n\n</eslint-code-block>\n\n<eslint-code-block :rules=\"{'vue/valid-model-definition': ['error']}\">\n\n```vue\n<script>\n/* ✗ BAD */\nexport default {\n  model: {\n    prop: 'list',\n    events: 'update'\n  }\n}\n</script>\n```\n\n</eslint-code-block>\n\n<eslint-code-block :rules=\"{'vue/valid-model-definition': ['error']}\">\n\n```vue\n<script>\n/* ✗ BAD */\nexport default {\n  model: {\n    props: 'list',\n    events: 'update'\n  }\n}\n</script>\n```\n\n</eslint-code-block>\n\n<eslint-code-block :rules=\"{'vue/valid-model-definition': ['error']}\">\n\n```vue\n<script>\n/* ✗ BAD */\nexport default {\n  model: {\n    name: 'checked',\n    props: 'list',\n    event: 'update'\n  }\n}\n</script>\n```\n\n</eslint-code-block>\n\n## :rocket: Version\n\nThis rule was introduced in eslint-plugin-vue v9.0.0\n\n## :mag: Implementation\n\n- [Rule source](https://github.com/vuejs/eslint-plugin-vue/blob/master/lib/rules/valid-model-definition.js)\n- [Test source](https://github.com/vuejs/eslint-plugin-vue/blob/master/tests/lib/rules/valid-model-definition.js)",
